Modifications (see docs/features/ai-chat-v2/adr/0010-build-the-ai-section-
from-own-chat-elements-ported-from-vercel-ai-elements-onto-base-ui.md):

- Rebuilt on @base-ui/react through this project's components/ui
  primitives (shadcn "base-vega" style) instead of Radix-based shadcn
  components; Radix-only APIs (asChild, Slot) replaced by Base UI's
  `render` prop or plain composition.
- conversation.tsx: driven by the project's useFollowLatest hook (48 px
  follow threshold, reduced motion, jump control) instead of
  use-stick-to-bottom; no role="log" (it would announce every streamed
  delta) - the scroll area is instead a labelled region ("Messages") and
  a Tab stop with a focus ring, which a keyboard jump focuses;
  ConversationContent is a full-width scroll area with a centred
  max-w-3xl column; ConversationDownload not ported.
- message.tsx: MessageResponse renders safe Markdown with react-markdown
  and remark-gfm (T62, ADR-0012; no streamdown, no raw HTML, no images,
  links only to in-app paths); MessageAvatar taken
  from the earlier upstream API; MessageAction shows a visible label;
  the branch selector and toolbar are not ported.
- prompt-input.tsx: no attachments, screenshots, referenced sources,
  action menu, model select, hover card, command palette or nanoid;
  the caller owns the text and its validation; the card is the project's
  InputGroup; an Enter keydown with keyCode 229 (WebKit's IME commit)
  never submits; the submit button shows a decorative spinner (no status
  region of its own) while a reply is in flight and sends no stop
  request.
- suggestion.tsx: wraps onto lines instead of a horizontal ScrollArea,
  and a long chip shrinks to the row and wraps its own text.
- loader.tsx: replaces upstream Shimmer (which needs motion) with the
  project's Spinner, static under prefers-reduced-motion.
- Styling adjusted to the project's design tokens and the AI section's
  screen manifest (docs/features/ai-chat-v2/screens.md).
